      "message": "Say each thing once and give the settings room\n\nThe head row owns the page title, its count and its actions; the\npages beneath no longer repeat the title. The repository page keeps\nits description and chips under the tabs, with room before the files,\nand the tags in the rail are rows. A long repository list gets a\nfilter with owner chips. New repository is the form on the page, not\na card in it. The theme control in the account menu is a row again.\n\nEvery select is a dropdown drawn in the page's own type, with the\nselect still underneath for the form and for no script. The\nrepository settings are panels that explain themselves: checks as\nswitches with a sentence each, approval and review domains, human\nlooks, earned trust with its threshold as a sentence, packs, and a\npanel to save or try the policy first.\n\nPasskeys: a synced passkey reports a counter of zero for ever, and\nthe library has already applied the clone rule, so sign-in no longer\nrefuses it. Registration asks for a discoverable credential, which is\nwhat puts iCloud Keychain on the menu, and sign-in sends the typed\nname.\n\nChange-Id: Iuxfix0139\nTask: t-7bzkyxm6zdynewfjw794qzc6c8\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
